# Start: turns_school_training's input.sav verbatim (France, Spring 1600, turn 108; England at peace,
# the Europe-bound Caravel held at sea, French units fortified, Quebec Schoolhouse + teacher).
# Covers: turn 109's King tax raise (+1% to 27%) refused through @TAXOPTIONS row 2 ("Hold 'Quebec
# Tobacco Party'"): @TEAPARTY dumps Quebec's 12 Tobacco (the stock before this turn's colony production:
# 3dc8 answers inside 5e52, before the 00f2 colony loop), the tax stays at 26%, Tobacco is boycotted
# (nations[1].boycott_bitmap bit 2); production then adds 4 more. Everything else as turns_school_training (Fisherman graduates).
key space                  # end turn 108
wait 30
key Return                 # Help: Time Scale (two turns per year from 1600)
wait 10
key Return                 # SoL in Quebec up to 60%: Continue turn
wait 10
key Return                 # price of Cigars rises
wait 10
shot                       # Autumn 1600: End of Turn
key space                  # end turn 109
wait 30
key Return                 # Iroquois gift of 16 Ore to Port au Prince
wait 6
                           # King raises tax by 1% to 27% (@KINGTAX variant: tenth wife)
key Down                   # @TAXOPTIONS row 2: Hold 'Quebec Tobacco Party'
key Return
wait 6
key Return                 # @TEAPARTY: 12 tons of Tobacco into the sea at Quebec, Tobacco boycotted
wait 6
key Return                 # SoL in Port au Prince 12%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return                 # SoL in Martinique 51%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return                 # SoL in Guadeloupe 70%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return                 # Horses cargo ready at Montreal (warehouse full): Continue turn
wait 6
key Return                 # @TRAINPROFESSION: a colonist in Quebec has learned Fisherman
wait 10
shot                       # Spring 1601: End of Turn
